Evergreen-Patch: installer-stub-from-branding
Why: The installer .exe is a 7-Zip self-extracting stub followed by the
  packaged files, so Windows shows the stub's icon for it: Firefox's stub
  carries the Firefox logo. Take the stub from the branding directory,
  where `eg.py prepare` writes a copy with Evergreen's icon
  (tools/eg/sfxstub.py).
Upstream: not upstreamable (Mozilla ships one brand's stub)
Drop-when: Firefox takes the stub's icon from the branding directory
Owner: Evergreen maintainers

--- a/browser/installer/windows/Makefile.in
+++ b/browser/installer/windows/Makefile.in
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 ifeq ($(TARGET_CPU), aarch64)
 SFX_MODULE = $(topsrcdir)/other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/7zSD.ARM64.sfx
 else
-SFX_MODULE = $(topsrcdir)/other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/7zSD.Win32.sfx
+SFX_MODULE = $(topsrcdir)/$(MOZ_BRANDING_DIRECTORY)/7zSD.Win32.sfx
 endif
 
 INSTALLER_FILES = \
